		<name>SuperAwesomeMagicalHealth</name>
		<summary>Your own health server's app: scores, wearables, food, mood, cycle and more</summary>
		<desc>&lt;p&gt;The phone app for &lt;b&gt;SuperAwesomeMagicalHealth&lt;/b&gt;, a health server you run yourself. Your data stays on your server, and the private parts are encrypted there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Scores like Oura's.&lt;/b&gt; Readiness, sleep and activity against your own baseline, with plain-English insights, stress and resilience, and trends over weeks and months.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Your wearables, on your server.&lt;/b&gt; Colmi rings over Bluetooth, Pebble and Garmin through Gadgetbridge, anything in Health Connect, and blood pressure monitors and glucose meters. The app carries their readings to your server.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Log what matters to you.&lt;/b&gt; Food (with barcode scanning), water, coffee and alcohol, weight, workouts, and how you feel. Turn on what else you want to keep track of:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mood, a private journal, check-ins (PHQ-9, GAD-7) and calming tools, with support lines one tap away&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your cycle, with predictions, and pregnancy, after a birth, perimenopause and menopause&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bladder and bowel diary with pelvic floor exercises&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medications with reminders, injection-site rotation and lab results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Blood pressure and glucose, symptoms and migraines, habits, hormone therapy and appointments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Reminders that work offline&lt;/b&gt;, a weekly digest, reports for your doctor, and read-only sharing with someone who cares for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You need a SuperAwesomeMagicalHealth server to sign in to: it runs in Podman or Docker (see the source code's README).&lt;/p&gt;
</desc>
